# Supabase dev/staging database. Copy to .env.supabase (gitignored) and paste
# the project's database password; `just server-supabase` sources this file.
#
# A47: dev and early staging ONLY. The free tier's 500 MB cannot hold this
# pgvector workload, so production needs its own Postgres.
#
# Shape of the URL:
#   - session pooler on 5432, not the transaction pooler on 6543 (sqlx uses
#     prepared statements, which transaction-mode pooling does not carry)
#   - user is `postgres.<project-ref>`
#   - the direct host `db.<project-ref>.supabase.co` is IPv6-only, hence the pooler
#
# Setup, and the Data API lockout that must be re-applied whenever the project is
# recreated, are in README.md § Supabase dev database.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres.<project-ref>:<db-password>@aws-0-<region>.pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres?sslmode=require
